# What the CLI is allowed to upload.
#
# `vercel deploy` uploads the working directory, not the git tree, so anything
# sitting locally ships unless it is listed here. Several directories in this
# project are deliberately untracked because they carry credentials and client
# data — without this file a manual deploy would push them to Vercel.

# Audit notes describing open vulnerabilities, and ad-account data (92 MB).
audit-tu-tesis-rd/
ads-tu-tesis-rd/

# Lead scraper: plaintext API token and scraped personal data.
scripts/scrapers/

# Local secrets. Real values belong in Vercel's environment variables.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Agent tooling and run artifacts.
.omx/
.codex/
.claude/
.agent/
temp_skills_repo/
graphify-out/
src/graphify-out/
.unlighthouse/

# Build inputs and reports that the deployment does not need.
node_modules/
_backup_legacy/
web-para-subir/
tutesisrd-dashboard/
docs/
*.log

# Build and error logs dropped at the repo root (build_log.txt, tsc_errors.txt,
# test_output.txt…). Anchored to the root on purpose: an unanchored `*.txt`
# also swallowed `public/robots.txt`, and because the SPA rewrite sends every
# unmatched path to `/`, production answered /robots.txt with the HTML shell
# instead of 404 — so the breakage was invisible. Keep the anchor, and keep the
# guard below.
/*.txt
!public/robots.txt
